  "description": "All English majors share a common foundation of coursework in linguistics, literature, and writing that effectively anchor learning in the integrated art, craft, and science of language. Students develop skills with which to engage story, practice interpretation, and experience the cultural and historical diversity of language and literature. Students in the writing concentration choose additional courses focusing on specific genres (e.g., fiction or journalism), audiences (e.g., children or adolescent readers), and purposes (e.g., journalism or business writing). Students who pursue English as an additional major may waive ENGL 395, 2 semester hours of electives, and the experiential requirement (ENGL 380, ENGL 390, or HNRS 399). Overlap Policy University policy does not allow students to pursue a major in more than one English concentration.",
